{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793710576,"nonce":"9P8I1AWYvW+qcnYJWNJprsz+A20=","title":"Buttons do not switch to the pointer cursor on hover, and resizable panel dividers show the wrong cursor","message":"Reported by the owner, 2026-11-03. Two symptoms of the same path, not yet investigated.\n\n- `cn::button` and other pressable controls keep the arrow cursor on hover; they should show the pointer (hand) cursor, as a browser does for a button.\n- The draggable divider of `cn::resizable` shows the wrong cursor: it should be the resize cursor for its axis (col-resize for a vertical divider, row-resize for a horizontal one).\n\nWhere to start\n- The cursor comes from the CSS `cursor` property (UA styles and the CN_STYLES rules) or from the builder's `cursor_*` methods; check that each of these controls sets one, and that the rule reaches the node (a class rule, `:hover`, and the node that receives the hit, which is often a child of the control).\n- The hover path has several independent gates that silently swallow a cursor. The memory note \"Hover cursor has six gates\" lists them for the rich-text case: the `has_any_cursor_style` pipeline gate, the `cursor_inside_last_leaf` early-out that skips the move pipeline while the pointer stays in one leaf, the ancestor walk in `get_cursor_at` using the hit leaf, and parent-relative layout locations. Instrument the runtime path (an `eprintln` behind an env var at each stage) rather than reasoning about which gate it is. Clicks working while the cursor does not is the clue.\n- Check whether this is a regression: the cursor rules may have moved from Rust builders into stylesheet rules during the cn restyle (button, resizable), and a rule keyed on a part the cursor lookup does not reach would explain both controls.\n\nTo do: reproduce headless (blinc_recorder Headless: hover the control, read the cursor the window would set), then fix and add a test per control; also check the Linux and web cursor paths separately.","files":null}]}